  "body": {
    "id": "lem:realizability-bound",
    "kind": "lemma",
    "statement": "Every jointly realizable continuous-rank primitive vector in \\(\\mathcal{M}\\) satisfies \\(A_s\\kappa_j/b_{1j}\\le5\\sqrt{15}/18\\), uniformly over active \\(j=(C,s)\\in J\\).",
    "free_symbols": [
      "A",
      "kappa",
      "b1",
      "J"
    ],
    "depends_on": [
      "ass:pair-spacing",
      "ass:primitive-compactness",
      "def:population-class"
    ],
    "justification": "This rules out a terminal pure-stage-2 plateau by linking Gaussian coordinates back to feasible finite populations.",
    "gap": "The bound combines pair-spacing density, variance, and rank covariance and is not present in the Gaussian optimization literature.",
    "consumer": "Endpoint optimality is certified over actual finite-population limits rather than an enlarged, potentially impossible Gaussian parameter box.",
    "proof_tex": "Fix a jointly realizable active stage-one block, center its empirical baseline law, and let its limiting variance and pair slope be \\(\\sigma^2>0\\) and \\(\\lambda>0\\).  Convolve the empirical law with the uniform density on an interval of width \\(\\delta_N=u_\\star/\\sqrt N\\), where \\([0,u_\\star]\\) is inside the pair-spacing window.  For the resulting density \\(f_N\\), the ordered-pair convention gives the exact overlap identity\n\\[\n\\|f_N\\|_2^2\n=\\frac{2}{N^2\\delta_N^2}\\int_0^{\\delta_N}K_N(u)\\,du\n=\\frac{2}{u_\\star^2}\\int_0^{u_\\star}N^{-3/2}K_N(x/\\sqrt N)\\,dx\n\\longrightarrow\\lambda.\n\\]\nIts variance is \\(\\sigma_N^2+\\delta_N^2/12\\), which tends to \\(\\sigma^2\\) by the variance and share premises.\n\nFor any centered density \\(f\\) of variance \\(\\sigma_f^2>0\\), take \\(a=\\sqrt5\\sigma_f\\) and \\(g(x)=3(1-x^2/a^2)_+/(4a)\\).  Since \\((1-x^2/a^2)_+\\ge1-x^2/a^2\\),\n\\[\n\\int fg\\ge\\frac{3}{5a},\n\\qquad\n\\int g^2=\\frac{3}{5a}.\n\\]\nThe inequality \\(\\int(f-g)^2\\ge0\\) gives \\(\\|f\\|_2^2\\sigma_f\\ge3/(5\\sqrt5)\\).  Applying it to \\(f_N\\) gives \\(\\lambda\\sigma\\ge3/(5\\sqrt5)\\).\n\nPair spacing removes asymptotic atoms, so the normalized midrank variance tends to \\(1/12\\).  Cauchy--Schwarz gives \\(\\operatorname{Cov}(B,U^0)\\le\\sigma/\\sqrt{12}\\).  Joint realizability and the definitions imply\n\\[\nA=\\frac{\\sqrt{r_1}}{2\\sigma},\\qquad\nb_1=\\sqrt3\\lambda\\sqrt{r_1},\\qquad\n\\kappa=\\frac{\\sqrt{12}\\operatorname{Cov}(B,U^0)}\\sigma.\n\\]\nConsequently\n\\[\n\\frac{A\\kappa}{b_1}\n=\\frac{\\operatorname{Cov}(B,U^0)}{\\sigma^2\\lambda}\n\\le\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{12}\\sigma\\lambda}\n\\le\\frac{5\\sqrt{15}}{18}.\n\\]\nAll denominators are positive by the primitive variance and pair-spacing conditions, and the argument is cellwise, hence uniform over finite \\(J\\).",
    "proof_basis": {
